{"version":1,"type":"session-summary","driving_event":"Issue #418 showed that aptove/swift-sdk 0.1.16 applies the backend’s 30-second default timeout to the full session/prompt request, even while session/update chunks continue, causing a healthy ACP backend to be marked unusable.","decision":"Use the SDK’s request-level timeout override for session/prompt with a one-hour deadline. Keep the protocol-layer default at 30 seconds for connection, handshake, and session operations. Add a fixture-backed public runTurn regression test with continuous updates across the former timeout boundary.","impact":"Changed ACP backend prompt request decoding and deadline only in GnosticACPAscendant, plus its test fixture and public-seam test. GnosticCore and dependency pins are unchanged. Existing cancellation and transport/process failure handling remain in place.","recurrence_control":"The regression runs a prompt for 31 seconds with streamed assistant chunks, asserts successful completion, and verifies the backend remains usable. make verify, make acp-smoke, make runner-smoke, and git diff --check passed.","rejected_alternatives":[],"sources":[]}
